- **Detailed Feature Specifications:** Provide detailed descriptions of how the scoring system works, how to implement saving/loading features, and how to handle invalid inputs or errors. This clarity will aid developers in understanding the expected behavior. (Source: 2nd and 3rd project results)  
- **Task Grouping for Clarity:** Group tasks by related functionalities, such as game logic and UI rendering, to streamline development and testing processes. This organization will help convey interdependencies and facilitate better workflow management. (Source: 2nd and 3rd project results)  
- **Unit Testing Integration:** Assign explicit unit testing tasks based on the game mechanics and UI functions, ensuring a robust testing strategy that accompanies feature implementation. (Source: 1st and 3rd project results)  
- **User Feedback Mechanisms:** Implement feedback mechanisms, such as displaying user messages when they win or lose, and provide options to restart or continue playing. This will enhance user engagement and improve the gaming experience. (Source: 3rd project result)  

By addressing these suggestions, the task plan can achieve improved clarity, reliability, and a more engaging user experience.
